Z||000000||Black88GT||03-02-2001||02:27 AM||||I *really* want a set of MSD wires, but who woulda thought that they don't make specific sets for Fiero's?!  Big surprise.  But I did see in my MSD Catalog that part number 3172 says "All 172(2.8L), 231(3.8L), 252(4.1L), Firebird, Phoenix, Sunbird, w/Dist."  Then under year it says "1976-1988".  So, why wouldn't this fit V6 Fiero's??  It says all 2.8's.  Just wanna check to make sure before I bought them.  <P>Also as an interesting note, MSD makes a billet Distributor for "Super Duty 4cyl." Looks sweet, part number 8490.  Wish they made them for V6 Fiero's...<P>[EDITED]<BR>Ahhh wait.  I just figured out something.  The P/N 3172 is not the 8.5mm MSD wires, its the crappy blue looking 8mm "Heli-Core" wires.  The Super Conductor wires are the ones I want, 8.5mm.  Now, it does list a universal set, P/N 31189, it says <P>"For engines with late model type (HEI "spark plug top") distributor caps.  Multi-Angle boots and terminals installed on one end.  90 degree disctributor boots and terminals included"<P>The only problem is, it says for 8 cylinder engines.  Would it work anyway? <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 03-02-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula88||03-02-2001||09:27 AM||||It should work in theory. The problem will come in because the spark plug boots won't fit into the factory heat shields, and without them, you may end up melting the boots and ruining the wires.  I've not tried a set of aftermarket wires, so I'm not sure if this is a serious problem or not.  Your mileage may vary.  Some settling may have ocurred during shipping.||||reg||6
